# Expense Tracker — Agent Instructions
## Stack
- Backend: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.x, SQLite (backend/app.db), Pydantic v2,
  PyJWT, bcrypt (use the bcrypt package directly, NOT passlib)
- Frontend: React + Vite, JavaScript (no TypeScript), react-router-dom, plain fetch.
  No UI library, no Tailwind.
- Tests: pytest + FastAPI TestClient using the conftest `client` fixture
  (fresh in-memory SQLite with StaticPool; tests must NOT touch backend/app.db)
## Layout
backend/app/{main.py,database.py,models.py,schemas.py,auth.py,routers/}
backend/tests/
frontend/src/{api.js,constants.js,App.jsx,pages/,components/}
backups/            <- timestamped SQLite backups (never committed to Git)
API.md   <- source of truth for every endpoint
PLAN.md  <- phase checklist
## Commands
- Backend: cd backend && python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate && pip install -r requirements.txt && uvicorn app.main:app --port 8100 --host 0.0.0.0
- Tests: cd backend && source .venv/bin/activate && pytest -q
- Frontend: cd frontend && npm install && npm run dev -- --port 5173 --host
- Frontend build: cd frontend && npm run build
## Rules
- Ports 8000, 8001, 3000 and 80 are used by other services. Use only 8100 and 5173.
- All backend routes are prefixed /api. Vite proxies /api to http://127.0.0.1:8100.
- API.md is the contract. Never change an endpoint without updating API.md first.
- Run the tests after every change. A phase is not done until pytest is green.
- Keep files under ~200 lines. One router per resource.
- Do not add dependencies that are not already listed without asking.
- No placeholder, stub or TODO code. Every endpoint must be fully implemented.
- Never delete/recreate backend/app.db for schema changes; use ensure_schema()
  in database.py to ALTER TABLE non-destructively.
- Do not reset user data without explicit user authorization; back up first
  (see backups/).

## Project-Specific Gotchas (learned during repairs)
- Login contract: POST /api/auth/login takes JSON {username, password}; the
  `username` field accepts the registered email OR username
  (routers/auth.py LoginRequest + auth.py get_user_by_identifier).
- Collection expense routes are /api/expenses/ (trailing slash). Calling
  /api/expenses triggers a 307 redirect whose Location is cross-origin through
  the Vite proxy; browsers then STRIP the Authorization header -> 401.
  Frontend collection calls must use '/api/expenses/'.
- Empty-string filter query params (e.g. min_amount=&end_date=) fail FastAPI
  validation with 422. frontend/src/api.js skips empty values before
  serializing; keep it that way.
- frontend/src/api.js formatApiError() turns FastAPI validation error ARRAYS
  into readable messages ("Username: Field required"). Never stringify error
  detail objects (produces "[object Object]"). Network failures map to a
  readable message too.
- ExpenseCreate.amount uses Field(gt=0): zero/negative amounts are rejected.
  401 responses have a STRING detail; 422 responses have an ARRAY detail.
- CORS: app/main.py pins allow_origins to http://20.20.20.152:5173,
  localhost:5173, 127.0.0.1:5173 - update if the LAN IP changes. The Vite
  proxy makes requests same-origin in normal dev use; CORS only matters for
  direct browser-to-8100 calls.
- httpx is pinned to 0.27.2 in requirements.txt: 0.28+ removed the `app=` kwarg
  that starlette 0.27's TestClient passes to httpx.Client.
- Tests use the conftest client fixture (in-memory SQLite + dependency
  override). A module-level TestClient(app) in test files defeats isolation
  and hits the real app.db - do not reintroduce that pattern.
- Categories for the Add Expense form come from frontend/src/constants.js
  (EXPENSE_CATEGORIES). The backend accepts any category string; keep the
  dropdown list as the single source to avoid inconsistent category names.
- Payment method is NOT a field in the model - do not add form fields for it.

## Work Completed (chronological)
1. CORS + proxy repair (2026-11-02): added CORSMiddleware to app/main.py;
   switched frontend to relative '/api' URLs so the Vite proxy is used.
   Fixed browser "OPTIONS /api/auth/register 405" and NetworkError.
2. Login contract repair (2026-11-02/03): replaced the form-encoded
   OAuth2PasswordRequestForm mismatch with a consistent JSON LoginRequest;
   login now accepts email or username; fixed frontend login() sending
   FormData with a JSON content-type header (the 422 root cause); readable
   error rendering (no more "[object Object],[object Object]").
3. Protected-route fix: frontend expense list/create use trailing-slash
   paths, eliminating the cross-origin 307 redirect that stripped the
   Authorization header (401 "Not authenticated").
4. Non-destructive schema migration: ensure_schema() adds missing columns
   (category, expense_date) to an existing app.db at startup.
5. Test suite repair: pinned httpx==0.27.2, switched tests to JSON login,
   wired tests to the conftest in-memory client fixture, added StaticPool.
   Suite is green (21 tests).
6. Authorized DB reset (2026-11-03): full SQLite backup to
   backups/app.db-20261103-020800.bak (contains the prior 10 users + 1
   expense), verified valid, then users/expenses tables emptied; schema and
   indexes preserved; app.db file kept.
7. Manual expense entry (2026-11-03): + Add Expense button and modal
   (AddExpenseModal.jsx / AddExpenseModal.css) with title, amount>0
   validation (client + backend Field(gt=0)), category dropdown, date
   defaulting to today, optional description; instant dashboard refresh
   (list, totals, monthly summary) with a success message.
8. Empty-filter 422 fix in api.js query-param serialization.
9. Documentation: README.md and backend/API.md updated (auth flow, expense
   fields, startup schema migration, backup location).

## Known Environment Issues
- AGENTS.md is owned by root; agents cannot edit it directly. This file is
  the staged replacement: apply it with
  `sudo cp AGENTS.md.new AGENTS.md`.
- Two integration-test accounts remain in app.db (usernames
  janedoe1793651991350 and bobby1793651992538, *.example.com emails).
  They don't block new registrations and can be deleted on request.
